# Grooves

A browser-based drum sequencer prototype built on the iBlokz stack (Snabbdom, RxJS, Web Audio).

**Live demo:** [alex-milanov.github.io/grooves](https://alex-milanov.github.io/grooves/)

## Features

- Step sequencer with configurable tracks, BPM, time signature, and resolution
- Sample library panel for browsing kits and assigning samples to tracks
- Track settings panel with per-track volume, mute, and a themed WaveSurfer waveform preview
- Waveform playback cursor synced to sequencer hits
- Theme families (pixel, terminal, studio, crm) with light/dark modes

## Development

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm start
```

Open the URL Parcel prints (usually `http://localhost:1234`).

```bash
pnpm run build   # production build to dist/
pnpm run check   # Biome lint + format
```

## Stack

- [Parcel](https://parceljs.org/) — bundler
- [Snabbdom](https://github.com/snabbdom/snabbdom) + [iblokz-snabbdom-helpers](https://github.com/iblokz/iblokz-snabbdom-helpers) — UI
- [iblokz-state](https://github.com/iblokz/iblokz-state) + RxJS — state
- Web Audio API + [wavesurfer.js](https://wavesurfer.xyz/) — playback and waveform

See [docs/theming.md](docs/theming.md) and [docs/linting.md](docs/linting.md) for more.

**Vision & integration ideas:** [`brainstorming/`](brainstorming/)  
**Planning:** [`planning/`](planning/)

